{"case_id":"C003","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["API protocol","state transition"],"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["decoder.restart_frame!","decoder.prepare_scan?","decoder.apply_progressive_idct!","decoder.load_mcu_blocks_for_single_component_smooth!"],"reason":"H0 exercises only initialization followed by decode_image_config, decode_frame_config, and decode_frame. It never calls the public decoder.restart_frame! entry point or decodes again after a restart. S1 makes that transition materially relevant by resetting block_smoothing_lowest_scan_al to 16 in restart_frame!, while prepare_scan? repopulates that state and apply_progressive_idct! uses it to select load_mcu_blocks_for_single_component_smooth!. Therefore stale, incorrectly reset, or incorrectly rebuilt progressive block-smoothing state across restart-and-redecode is not covered.","evidence":["fuzz_image_decoder calls wuffs_base__image_decoder__decode_image_config, then repeatedly calls decode_frame_config and decode_frame; no restart_frame call appears in H0.","S1 decoder.restart_frame! sets call_sequence to 0x28, restores saved quantization state, resets scan_count, and explicitly initializes every block_smoothing_lowest_scan_al[i][j] to 16.","S1 decoder.prepare_scan? writes scan_al into block_smoothing_lowest_scan_al[this.scan_comps_cselector[i]][j].","S1 decoder.apply_progressive_idct! reads block_smoothing_lowest_scan_al to decide whether block smoothing is applicable and whether to choose load_mcu_blocks_for_single_component_smooth."],"recommended_action":"Extend the JPEG harness with a hash-selected restart protocol: after reaching a valid post-configuration or post-frame state, call restart_frame with index 0 and fuzzed relevant io_position/source repositioning, then decode frame configuration and frame data again. Include progressive multi-scan inputs that drive both major and minor smoothing, plus invalid call-sequence and nonzero-index restart calls."}
